THIS IS THE MOST IMPORTANT TEST. It verifies the entire security fix works.

Before the fix: Same browser = same visitorId = SHARED DATA (BUG)
After the fix: Each user has unique userId = ISOLATED DATA (SECURE)

Test requires:
- Two test email addresses (use Playwright's mailbox or mock)
- Ability to sign out and sign in as different users
- Dashboard stats verification

Consider using test.serial to ensure order:
```typescript
test.describe.serial('User Data Isolation', () => {
  let userAEmail: string;
  let userBEmail: string;

  test.beforeAll(async () => {
    // Generate unique test emails
    userAEmail = `test-a-${Date.now()}@example.com`;
    userBEmail = `test-b-${Date.now()}@example.com`;
  });

  test('User A signs up and creates data', async ({ page }) => { ... });
  test('User A logs out', async ({ page }) => { ... });
  test('User B signs up and sees empty dashboard', async ({ page }) => { ... });
  // etc.
});
```
